---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import RoyRecommends1 from '../assets/RoyRecommends/InputController1.jpg';
import RoyRecommends2 from '../assets/RoyRecommends/InputController2.jpg';
import environmentBG from '../assets/RoyRecommends/robotcontrollerbase.png';
const pageTitle = "Kylan Curran";
---
<Layout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
<h2>Roy Recommends</h2>
 <p>
	"Roy Recommends" is an input controller that I developed in Spring 2025 as a play on "Simon Says."
	The project was created for a digital interativity course at the University of Oregon. I first 
	wired the controller using an Arduino microcontroller and switches. The controller accepts
	user input through movement of the robot's arms and head; when moved in the direction as 
	given on the screen, Roy indicates success. If the user moves in the incorrect 
	direction, or the incorrect limb is moved, Roy indicates failure.
 </p>
 <p>
	I programmed the controller using the Arduino IDE to read input from the switches, 
	then connected this to a Processing sketch that displays the prompts and feedback on screen and 
	designed a pixel art scene to represent Roy's environment in an arcade style game format. 
 </p>
 <p>Link to project demonstration: 
          <a
            href="https://www.youtube.com/shorts/YiuRN2-EFh4"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Roy Recommends
          </a>
 </p>
  <div class="image-wrapper">
    <Image 
      src={RoyRecommends1}
      alt="Roy Front"
      loading="eager"
      class="project-image"
    />
        <Image 
      src={RoyRecommends2}
      alt="Roy Back"
      loading="eager"
      class="project-image"
    />
  </div>  
    <div class="image-wrapper">
    <Image 
      src={environmentBG}
      alt="Roy Environment"
      loading="eager"
      class="project-image"
    />
	</div>

</Layout>